# memchentic Capture

## Gate

If memchentic is **not** connected/ready, **skip this entire rule** — no
memchentic writes. Complete the task normally.

## Default (when connected) — lean aggressive

- Save **after verification**, autonomously — do not wait for the user.
- Cap: usually **1–3** writes per turn when several distinct insights landed.
  Prefer strong entries over noise.
- Bias toward saving anything you would otherwise re-discover next session.
  Skip only when the turn taught nothing durable.

## Must save (after verification)

- Non-obvious bug: root cause + fix
- Architecture / decision with rationale and paths
- Failed approach + the condition that made it fail
- Stable user preference that affects future work
- Workflow that took investigation to rediscover
- Host / MCP / env quirk that is not obvious from code alone
- User correction that should stick across sessions
- Reusable “when X, do Y / avoid Z” guidance

Save in the same turn the insight is verified, or at final handoff —
whichever comes first. For long investigations, save the durable breakthrough
when established; do not save every intermediate step.

## Which tool

| Kind | Tool | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Durable record | `remember` | Pass a closed `type` (below); default is `note` |
| Reusable advice | `guide_write` | Near-dup **upserts** and raises confidence (no `force`) |
| Patch existing | `revise` | Title / body / type / tags / expiry / path hints |
| Move space | `relocate` | Explicit destination `space_id` UUID only |
| Delete | `forget` | Entries or guides this principal can write |

**Entry vs guide vs both**

- Durable record only → `remember`.
- Reusable “when X, do Y / avoid Z” → `guide_write`.
- Same insight is both a fact **and** a standing rule → write **both**.

## Entry types (closed)

Pick the best label on every `remember`. Do **not** leave the API default
`note` when a better type fits. Types are classification metadata — the
server does not run a different pipeline per type.

| Type | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| `fact` | Stable truth about the world or codebase |
| `preference` | How someone wants work done |
| `decision` | A choice and its rationale |
| `instruction` | Standing directive the agent should follow |
| `feedback` | Correction after a mistake |
| `insight` | Learned non-obvious finding |
| `note` | Catch-all when nothing else fits |

**Must-save → type (pick one)**

| Insight | Prefer |
| --- | --- |
| Stable “this is how it is” | `fact` |
| How the user wants work done | `preference` |
| “We decided …” + rationale | `decision` |
| Standing always/never directive | `instruction` |
| Correction after the agent erred | `feedback` |
| Bug root cause + fix / hard-won quirk | `insight` |
| None of the above | `note` |

Guides are **not** an entry type — use `guide_write` for reusable advice.

## Write target

First match wins (case-insensitive exact group name; never invent a name):

1. `space_id` — UUID you already know (membership / admin access).
2. `group: "<name>"` — exact name from `me` memberships.
3. `visibility: "shared"` — caller’s default shared group, else their only
   group; otherwise error (save personal and say so, or ask once).
4. Nothing → **personal**.

Call `me` before a shared write when memberships or
`default_shared_space_id` are unknown. Default shared group is set via REST /
GUI (`PATCH /api/me`), not MCP.

`ADMIN_API_KEY` is a real `ADMIN_EMAIL` user: omit-space → that user’s
**personal** space; `space_create` is allowed. Prefer a **per-user API key or
JWT** for normal agent sessions — admin list/search is instance-wide.

## Remember-only knobs

- `path_hint` / `repo_hint` — path-scoped insights so `about_path` / `find`
  can find them later (not on `guide_write`).
- `force` — override near-dup refusal on **`remember` only**. Near-dup on
  `guide_write` upserts; do not invent a `force` flag for guides.
- `tags`, `expires_at` — optional on `remember`; `revise` can `clear_expiry`.

## Refuse

- No transient status, todos, raw logs, guesses, generic programming
  knowledge, code-obvious facts, chat dumps, or one-shot noise.
- **Never** store secrets, credentials, tokens, private personal data, or
  unredacted production payloads.
- **Never** invent another user’s identity or pass a client-supplied user id
  for ACL. Server principals only.
- Do not paste secret values the user put in chat into `remember` /
  `guide_write`.

## Hygiene

When overlap is plausible, call `overlap_report` (read-only), then merge via
`revise` / `forget` — never auto-delete. Report pairs are same-title in a
space; `conflicts` may be empty. Expiry is metadata — search does not hide
expired rows; extend or `clear_expiry` via `revise` when needed.
